    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: when an owner is created, return `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nBoth the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) responses flow through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, so I added the field once at the mapping layer:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (and it's excluded from request bodies).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes `displayName` from the stored entity: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` (creates an owner with first name \"John\", reads it back, expects `\"<lastName>, John\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
